WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:01.590
Hey David.

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:07.850
Bernie has been saying that on day one he
will legalize marijuana.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:10.530
Is this actually possible?

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.790
I sort of have dealt with this before.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.209
When a caller asked about it, I it's not possible.

00:00:16.209 --> 00:00:21.911
So what it really comes down to is when a
presidential candidate says on day one, I

00:00:21.911 --> 00:00:28.390
will do this, that the other thing, do they
literally mean on their first day or I guess

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:29.539
the first day is the inauguration.

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:31.770
Do they, do they mean their first day in the
office?

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:36.140
Which would be the second day or do they mean
this is generally going to be a priority of

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.140
mine?

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.100
Because the reality is that when it comes
to something like legalizing marijuana, the

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:49.910
executive branch certainly could move a drug
from controlled substances schedule one by

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:53.520
directing the DEA to do it.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.120
Even if they did that, it doesn't happen in
one day.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.980
It takes longer.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:02.090
But even if you do it after a few days or
realistically, it's something that would take

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:03.720
weeks or months.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:10.560
It doesn't undo state level bands on cannabis
and you can't cancel those with an executive

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.560
order.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:16.560
This actually has a lot to do with a state's
rights versus the federal government.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:27.249
So Bernie could say on day one, I have directed
my attorney general not to do any, um, prosecution

00:01:27.249 --> 00:01:30.060
raids, any, anything at all.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:35.130
Uh, when it comes to cannabis in any state,
regardless of whether that state has or has

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:36.630
not legalized cannabis.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:42.599
So remember under Barack Obama's administration,
Obama directed the justice department not

00:01:42.599 --> 00:01:50.039
to go into States where marijuana was legal,
despite it continuing to be illegal federally.

00:01:50.039 --> 00:01:53.539
Bernie could say, we're going to apply that
to every state.

00:01:53.539 --> 00:01:56.819
Even in Idaho where cannabis is illegal.

00:01:56.819 --> 00:02:02.109
I still don't want federal agencies going
in there and enforcing a federal drug policy

00:02:02.109 --> 00:02:03.270
or whatever.

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:06.890
That's not a change to the law, but it does
change the enforcement.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:13.819
But if cannabis is illegal in Idaho, Idaho
police can continue to prosecute that and

00:02:13.819 --> 00:02:18.010
to police it regardless of what it is that
Bernie signs in the oval office.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:25.180
So what Bernie could relatively quickly do
would be immediately direct his attorney general

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:32.349
not to, uh, police cannabis in any state could
start the process of rescheduling cannabis

00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:34.490
away from schedule one.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:35.620
But that's, that's basically it.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:39.159
So the real question comes down to, it's actually
a semantic question.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:43.820
When a candidate says, I will do X, Y, orZ
on day one, what does that really mean?

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:44.930
Does it, does it mean day one?

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:45.930
Does it mean day two?

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:46.930
Does it mean the first month?

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:47.969
Does it mean the first year?

00:02:47.969 --> 00:02:48.969
Let me know what you think.

00:02:48.969 --> 00:02:52.930
And if you believe I am misunderstanding the
law around this, I of course would love to

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:53.299
hear from you as well.

